## Rule: Generate Session Summaries

Whenever you dump, export, or save Jules session or activity data (JSON files containing `activities` or `sessions` arrays), you MUST also generate a companion **summary file**.

### Why

- Full activity/session files can be hundreds of MB with embedded git diffs
- Summaries enable quick review without loading massive files
- The standard is defined in `docs/guides/session_summary_standard.md`

### Summary File Requirements

| Property       | Requirement                                                                 |
|---------------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| **Format**    | YAML (.yaml)                                                                |
| **Location**  | Same directory as the full JSON file                                        |
| **Naming**    | `<full_filename>_summary.yaml` (e.g., `activities_123_summary.yaml`)         |
| **Max size**  | 50 KB                                                                        |

### Required Summary Fields

Every summary MUST include:

```yaml
session:
  id: "<session-id>"
  title: "<session title>"
  repository: "<repo name>"
  created: "<ISO 8601 timestamp>"
  updated: "<ISO 8601 timestamp>"
  status: "<completed|failed|in_progress|awaiting_approval|awaiting_feedback|paused|unknown>"
  source: "<pr|issue|manual>"
```

### Recommended Summary Fields

Include these when available:

```yaml
purpose: "<brief goal description (max 500 chars)>"
summary: "<narrative of what happened (max 2000 chars)>"
participants:
  - role: "user|agent"
    message: "<truncated message (max 200 chars)>"
changes:
  - file: "<file path>"
    summary: "<change description (max 200 chars)>"
    change_type: "<added|modified|deleted|renamed>"
plan:
  steps:
    - "<step description>"
pr:
  url: "<PR URL>"
  title: "<PR title>"
errors:
  - type: "<error type>"
    message: "<error message>"
```

### What NOT to include in summaries

- ❌ Full `unidiffPatch` git diffs (keep in the full file)
- ❌ Complete conversation transcripts (keep in the full file)
- ❌ Raw API response metadata (keep in the full file)
- ❌ Redundant timestamp snapshots (keep only in the full file)

### How to Generate

Use the automation script:

```bash
# Single file
python scripts/generate_session_summaries.py activities_123.json

# Entire directory
python scripts/generate_session_summaries.py /path/to/activities/

# Force regenerate
python scripts/generate_session_summaries.py --force /path/to/activities/
```

### Compliance

- [ ] Summary file created alongside full data file
- [ ] Summary follows YAML format
- [ ] All required fields present
- [ ] No full diffs or transcripts leaked into summary
- [ ] Summary file size < 50 KB
- [ ] Summary tracked in git (full file may be gitignored)

